From 847215f1657278fd2d46e24ddd8ba84151c47a4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jm-v7 030: Bifrost restart in the GS emulation, per-viewport
 depth, VS viewport index, large tessellation, tess/GS point size

Builds (NDK r30, RC5-dev-v7G-B b1). Not device-tested yet.

- Primitive restart (A06 fill_mode *_restart_*, geometry *_restart_*):
  the emulation assembled strips/fans by position and ignored restart.
  A serial libpan kernel, panlib_v7_gs_restart_list(), cuts an indexed
  strip/fan/strip-adjacency draw with restart into restart-free runs and
  writes their primitives as a 32-bit list plus a new indexed indirect
  command; the emulation (and the 0017 polygon passthrough) then
  assembles a plain list.
- gs_viewport_depth: the tiler had the union of the viewports' depth
  ranges. When the GS-selectable viewports' depth ranges differ, each
  viewport gets its own copy of the emulation index list and its own
  tiler job with its own VIEWPORT descriptor (panvk_gs_push::vp_split).
  Limit: primitives of different viewports with overlapping scissors are
  not drawn in API order.
- vs_viewport_index: a last pre-raster VS/TES writing gl_ViewportIndex
  is compiled for clip space and drawn through the passthrough GS; the
  index travels in PANVK_GS_VIEWPORT_INDEX_SLOT and becomes
  gl_ViewportIndex again in the passthrough. shaderOutputViewportIndex
  is exposed on v6/v7.
- Tessellation caps (px=682 = 2^20/1536, px=16 = 8192*3/1536):
  PANVK_TESS_MAX_INDICES 1M -> 8M, arena 64 -> 160 MB (growable),
  PANVK_TESS_GS_MAX_PRIMS 8192 -> 2M with the tess eval draw's GS
  emulation buffers from a new growable GPU-only cmdbuf pool (gs_pool),
  indirect varying buffer 2M -> 4M vertices (growable).
- shaderTessellationAndGeometryPointSize on v6/v7: TES point mode uses
  its gl_PointSize, GS point output writes an FP32 point size array,
  GS/TCS read gl_in[].gl_PointSize from the VS fp16 buffer, the point
  passthrough forwards it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
